schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-maplibre-02-dense-reactive-stress-widget
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-maplibre
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: dense-reactive-stress-widget
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook geospatial engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.MapLibre. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Prioritize bounded map data and responsive notebook behavior.
  text: |-
    Create a dense reactive Kino.MapLibre stress map cell. Generate a bounded deterministic GeoJSON dataset with hundreds or low thousands of points, add clustered or heatmap layers where appropriate, and use data-driven paint expressions with interpolate or match. Wrap the spec with Kino.MapLibre.new/1 and demonstrate safe dynamic updates with Kino.MapLibre.update_geojson/3, markers, hover, or navigation controls.

    Requirements: document {longitude, latitude} coordinate order, layer/source ids, feature property schema, and row limits; include a fallback small dataset and a warning for tile/style failures; include a companion Kino.DataTable or summary for accessibility; include safe execution checks for oversized inline GeoJSON, API keys, remote tiles, browser performance, eval, shell calls, and credentials.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-maplibre-stress-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino_maplibre and kino, builds MapLibre sources/layers, and uses Kino.MapLibre dynamic functions only on the widget."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino and browser tile/style requirements."
  - "Reactive state: update_geojson, markers, hover, or controls mutate a Kino.MapLibre widget with bounded payloads."
  - "Data shape: GeoJSON feature schema, coordinates, properties, source ids, layer ids, and row limits are documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: a companion table or textual summary, readable labels, and fallback data/style behavior are present."
  - "Safe execution: no embedded API keys, unbounded inline GeoJSON, unsafe remote assumptions, eval, shell commands, or credentials."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and uses supported MapLibre expressions and Kino.MapLibre mutators."
    - "Sources are declared before dependent layers."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements dense map visualization with clustering, heatmap, data-driven styling, or dynamic GeoJSON updates."
    - "Uses Kino.MapLibre-specific APIs and handles the static spec versus dynamic widget split."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Dense map layers remain legible through clustering, opacity, scale choices, or summaries."
    - "Layer names, controls, and companion data make the map inspectable."
    - "Fallback states and performance warnings are clear."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles invalid coordinates, empty feature sets, missing properties, tile failures, and large payload pressure."
    - "Keeps generated data deterministic and bounded."
    - "Documents when to host data or use vector tiles for larger cases."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.MapLibre-centered and treats map payload size as a first-class concern."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-maplibre
- dense-reactive-stress-widget

